+    "sections": {
+      "Printed source": "Wizards of the Coast, Revised v3.5 SRD, MonstersAnimals.rtf, Crocodile, Giant, and Crocodile combat. https://www.d20srd.org/srd/monsters/crocodile.htm#giantCrocodile",
+      "Attack": "Bite +11 melee for 2d8 + 12 damage, or Tail Slap +11 melee for 1d12 + 12 damage.",
+      "Full attack": "One Bite +11 melee for 2d8 + 12 damage, or one Tail Slap +11 melee for 1d12 + 12 damage.",
+      "Special qualities": "Hold Breath (Ex). It can hold its breath for four times its Constitution score, or 76 rounds, before it risks drowning.\nLow-light vision. See twice as far as a human in dim illumination while retaining color and detail.",
+      "Skills and feats": "Skills. Hide +1, Listen +5, Spot +5, Swim +16. In water, add a +4 racial bonus to Hide. At the surface with only eyes and nostrils exposed, it also gets +10 cover to Hide. The +8 racial Swim bonus applies to special actions and hazards. It can take 10 on Swim while distracted or endangered, and can run when swimming in a straight line.\nFeats. Alertness, Endurance, Skill Focus (Hide). Endurance adds +4 to Constitution checks to hold breath after the listed interval.",
+      "Encounter ecology": "Environment. Warm marshes, Salt water. Organization. Solitary or colony (6–11). Giant crocodiles use the smaller crocodile’s ambush behavior, waiting low in the water and trying to drag a grabbed victim deeper. Treasure none. Advancement. 8–14 HD (Huge). Level adjustment none listed.",
+      "Special attacks": "Improved Grab (Ex). After it hits a Large or smaller foe with Bite, the crocodile can immediately attempt a grapple as a free action without a touch attack or an attack of opportunity. On a win, it draws the target into its space and may drag it if the victim is within its drag limit. It can grapple normally or hold with its jaws at −20 on grapple checks to avoid becoming grappled itself. Winning the initial grab adds no damage. Later successful grapple checks with the hold deal Bite damage. The crocodile uses opposed grapple checks to pin or move a struggling target.",
+      "At the table": "A target escapes with an opposed grapple check in place of an attack or a standard-action Escape Artist check against the crocodile’s grapple check. Escaping a pin leaves the target in the grapple. After the crocodile’s breath-holding interval, use escalating Constitution checks beginning at DC 10. Failure starts drowning, with 0 HP and unconsciousness on the first round, −1 HP on the next, and death on the third."
+    }
