+    "habitats": ["Cold aquatic"],
+    "sections": {
+      "Printed source": "Revised v3.5 SRD, MonstersDi-Do.rtf, DIRE SHARK and its following combat text. https://olimot.github.io/srd-v3.5/monsters/monsters-di-do.html#dire-shark",
+      "Attack": "Bite +18 melee (2d8 + 9).",
+      "Full attack": "Bite +18 melee (2d8 + 9).",
+      "Special attacks": "Improved Grab (Ex). A Bite hit lets it attempt a grapple as a free action with no touch attack or attack of opportunity. The general Improved Grab size limit applies because the entry gives no wider limit. Winning the check holds the creature and sets up Swallow Whole on the following round.\nSwallow Whole (Ex). Make a new grapple check to swallow a held Large or smaller foe. If swallowed, it takes 2d6 + 6 bludgeoning plus 1d8 + 4 acid each round. Cutting out requires a light slashing or piercing weapon to deal 25 damage to the digestive tract (AC 13). The wound closes after that creature leaves. The general Swallow Whole rules also deal bite damage on swallowing, count the prey as grappled, and return prey that escape the grapple to the shark’s mouth.\nGullet capacity. Two Large, eight Medium or Small, thirty-two Tiny, one hundred twenty-eight Diminutive, or five hundred twelve Fine or smaller opponents.",
+      "Special qualities": "Keen Scent (Ex). Can detect creatures by scent within 180 ft. and detect blood in water up to 1 mile away. Aquatic subtype. Breathes underwater only and uses its swim speed without routine Swim checks. The stat block lists Keen Scent. The general Animal rules grant low-light vision unless the specific entry overrides it.",
