+      "Full attack": "Bite +6 melee (1d8 + 6) or tail slap +6 melee (1d12 + 6).",
+      "Special attacks": "Improved Grab (Ex). After a bite hits, the crocodile can attempt a grapple as a free action. It needs no touch attack and provokes no attack of opportunity. The default size limit is at least one category smaller, so Small or smaller. If the crocodile wins, it holds the target in its jaws, drags it into deep water and tries to pin it on the bottom. The crocodile can pull a held target into its space and move with it if it can drag the target, without provoking for the pull. The initial hold adds no damage. Later successful grapple checks deal bite damage. It can hold with its jaws alone at −20 on grapple checks. With that option it can keep its Dexterity bonus to AC, threaten normally and use any remaining attacks on other foes.",
+      "Special qualities": "Hold Breath (Ex). It can hold its breath for 68 rounds (4 × Constitution 17) before risking drowning. Low-light vision doubles normal human sight distance in dim light and retains color and detail.",
+      "Skills and feats": "Hide +7, Listen +4, Spot +4, Swim +12. Alertness, Skill Focus (Hide). It gains a +4 racial Hide bonus in water and a +10 cover bonus while only its eyes and nostrils are exposed. The +8 racial Swim bonus applies to special maneuvers and hazards. The animal can take 10 even under threat and can run while swimming in a straight line.",
+      "Encounter ecology": "Ambushes prey while mostly submerged in a warm river or marsh. Encounter one or a colony of 6–11. Advancement 4–5 HD (Medium). No treasure or listed level adjustment."
+    }
