+      "Combat statistics": "Initiative +2. AC 16 (+4 size, +2 Dexterity), touch 14, flat-footed 12. Base attack +2, grapple none. Space 10 ft., reach 0 ft.",
+      "Attack": "Swarm. Automatically deal 1d6 damage to each creature whose space the swarm occupies at the end of its move. There is no attack roll or miss chance from cover or concealment.",
+      "Full attack": "Swarm. Automatically deal 1d6 damage to each creature whose space the swarm occupies at the end of its move. There is no attack roll or miss chance from cover or concealment.",
+      "Special attacks": "Distraction (Ex). A living creature that starts its turn in the swarm’s space must make a DC 11 Fortitude save or be nauseated for 1 round. The general subtype limits this to creatures vulnerable to the swarm’s damage. A nauseated creature can take only one move action per turn. Casting or concentrating on spells in the swarm requires a Concentration check at DC 20 + spell level. Skills demanding concentration require a DC 20 Concentration check.\nWounding (Ex). A living creature damaged by the swarm then loses 1 HP per round from bleeding. Additional wounds do not increase the rate. A DC 10 Heal check, a cure spell, or other healing magic stops it.",
+      "Special qualities": "Blindsense (Ex). Locate creatures within 20 ft. Total concealment still applies unless the swarm can actually see them. Swarm damage ignores concealment.\nLow-light vision. See twice as far as a human in dim light.\nSwarm traits. One pool of HP and one set of saves. Occupy a shared, shapeable 10-ft. space and fit through gaps large enough for one bat. Entering or moving through a hostile space provokes as normal. The swarm never threatens or makes opportunity attacks. It cannot grapple and is unaffected by grappling, trips, bull rushes, critical hits, or flanking. Effects aimed at a fixed number of creatures do not affect it, subject to the hive-mind exception for mind-affecting effects. Area effects deal 50% more damage. At 0 HP it disperses. It does not become staggered or dying. If rendered unconscious by nonlethal damage, it disperses until HP exceed that damage. Resolve strong wind against Diminutive size.\nWeapon damage. Use weapon damage immunity under the shared subtype rule, supported by the 2006 Monster Manual errata. The SRD entry still has the earlier half-damage line.\nShared swarm vulnerabilities. A lit torch used as an improvised weapon deals 1d3 fire damage on a hit. A thrown lit lantern deals 1d4 fire damage to creatures in adjacent squares where it breaks. Energy damage from a weapon can still apply if the weapon’s ordinary damage does not.",
+      "Skills and feats": "Listen +11, Spot +11. Each includes a +4 racial bonus that is lost if blindsense is negated.\nFeats: Alertness, Lightning Reflexes.",
+      "Encounter ecology": "Temperate deserts. Solitary, flight of 2–4 swarms, or colony of 11–20 swarms. No treasure or advancement. Level adjustment —. Nocturnal and never found aboveground in daylight. It tries to surround warm-blooded prey.",
+      "Printing conflicts": "Armor Class. The table prints touch 14 and flat-footed 12. Its listed +4 size and +2 Dexterity would give touch 16 and flat-footed 14 using the standard AC rules.\nWeapon damage. The Bat Swarm table lists half damage from slashing and piercing. The shared Diminutive Swarm subtype grants immunity to all weapon damage, confirmed for the Bat Swarm in the 17 February 2006 Monster Manual v3.5 errata. Use immunity at the table. "
+    }
