+      "Printed source": "Wizards of the Coast, Revised v3.5 SRD, MonstersS.rtf, RAT SWARM. https://www.d20srd.org/srd/monsters/swarm.htm#ratSwarm",
+      "Attack": "Swarm, 1d6 plus disease. At the end of its movement, deal damage automatically to each creature whose space it shares. There is no attack roll or miss chance for concealment or cover. The attack is nonmagical.",
+      "Full attack": "Swarm, 1d6 plus disease. The automatic Swarm Attack uses the same rules in both entries.",
+      "Special attacks": "Disease (Ex). Filth fever is delivered by the swarm attack. Make an immediate DC 12 Fortitude save to prevent infection. On a failure, after 1d3 days take 1d3 Dex and 1d3 Con damage. Save at DC 12 daily afterward or repeat the ability damage. Two successes in a row clear the disease.\nDistraction (Ex). A living creature that begins its turn in the swarm’s square makes a DC 12 Fortitude save or is nauseated for 1 round. A nauseated creature can take only one move action per turn and cannot attack, cast spells or concentrate. The shared subtype wording specifies living creatures vulnerable to the swarm’s damage. Both printed triggers are recorded here.",
+      "Special qualities": "Low-light vision. See twice as far as a human in dim light, with color and detail.\nScent. Detect by smell out to 30 ft., 60 ft. upwind or 15 ft. downwind. Double those ranges for strong odors and triple them for overpowering odors. A move action gives the direction. Pinpoint the source within 5 ft.\nTiny swarm. Halve damage from slashing and piercing weapons. It cannot be critically hit or flanked. The swarm cannot grapple or be grappled, tripped, or bull rushed. It breaks up at 0 HP or below and does not become staggered or dying from damage. Losing HP above 0 does not reduce its attack or defenses.",
+      "Swarm movement": "One nonflying Tiny swarm represents about 300 rats and uses one set of stats and saves. It can cover any four contiguous squares and fit through gaps a constituent rat can use. It shares spaces with creatures of any size and can pass through them. Moving into or through an opponent’s space can provoke an attack of opportunity. The swarm does not threaten creatures or make attacks of opportunity.",
+      "Swarm spell and effect rules": "Immune to effects that target a fixed number of creatures. The shared mind-affecting exception requires intelligence and a hive mind, and this block lists no hive mind. Area effects deal 50% extra damage. Casting a spell or maintaining concentration in the swarm’s area requires a Concentration check at DC 20 + spell level. Skills requiring patience or focus require a DC 20 Concentration check. An improvised lit torch deals 1d3 fire on a hit, and a broken thrown lit lantern deals 1d4 fire in adjacent squares. A weapon’s added energy damage applies in full. Sufficient damage reduction and incorporeality can prevent the swarm attack’s ordinary damage.",
+      "Nonlethal dispersal": "If nonlethal damage renders the swarm unconscious it disperses until its HP exceed its nonlethal damage.",
+      "Skills and feats": "Balance +10, Climb +10, Hide +14, Listen +6, Spot +7, Swim +10. Racial bonuses are +4 on Hide and Move Silently, +8 on Balance, Climb and Swim. The swarm uses Dex for Climb and Swim. It can take 10 on Climb and Swim even under pressure and can run while swimming straight. Feats are Alertness and Weapon Finesse.",
+      "Encounter ecology": "Any environment. Solitary, pack of 2–4 swarms, or infestation of 7–12 swarms. It surrounds warm-blooded prey. No advancement, level adjustment, or treasure.",
+      "Printed discrepancies": "The RTF gives 13 HP for 4d8, whose usual mean is 18. Use the listed HP 13. The creature and subtype use different phrasing for the Distraction trigger, as shown above."
+    }
